Z||000001||Monkeyman||05-13-2000||10:23 AM||||Last I heard (a couple of months ago), Eddie was still looking for someone in the states to sell/market his dash.  He said that he has about 50 offers.  I guess he's trying to choose the best one.  I hope everything goes OK, 'cause I just have to have one.  I don't care if I have to sell my clothes to finance it!  Best damn looking dash I have ever seen in a Fiero!  Maybe someone else has some more up to date info.  Then again, I might email him and ask myself.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fret Naught||05-14-2000||12:57 AM||||That is sure sweet looking, I'll bet it cost more than I paid for the whole car! be interesting to see what they are marketed for.||||reg||14
Z||000003||william_thorniii||05-15-2000||05:33 PM||||Eddy will be selling his molds sometime in the next few months.  They are complete now.  This is all that I know.  He seems to be leaving pricing up to the individuals that get their hands on the molds.  I guess we will all find out soon enough. <P>William T. Thorn, III<p>[This message has been edited by william_thorniii (edited 05-16-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000004||Monkeyman||05-20-2000||01:10 PM||||Just got an email from Eddy the other day.  Apparently he's a little worried that someone will try to gouge us on the price.  It seems like he's much more interested in seeing others with his dash than making tons of money.  The only name he's mentioned is a Scott Tilden.  Anybody know who he is???  Is anyone out there able/willing to produce these from a mold??  I first thought of Tom, but I know he's awfully busy.  Who else can do the job and has the time?  Not that I can afford one right now (but definitely on my wish list! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), but I'd sure like to see a worthwhile, trustworthy person produce these.  I'm thinking someone other than a V8Archie type who just seems to be out there for the $$.||||reg||1
